invariant: INV-16
file: poly1305_vector.h
catches: test/chacha-builds.sh
reason: poly1305_vector.h turns the vector Poly1305 on under
  CH_CHACHA_VECTOR alone, so a CHACHA=vector object whose builder never
  stated the widening multiply's timing runs UMULL, UMLAL or PMULUDQ on
  the one-time key, where ct.h's 16x16 decomposition belongs. Every
  vector still passes: the tags are the same, only the claim is gone. The
  script compiles poly1305.c under -DCH_CHACHA_VECTOR alone and requires
  that its object not call poly1305_vector_blocks.

--- old
#if defined(CH_CHACHA_VECTOR) && defined(CH_WIDEMUL_NATIVE)
--- new
#if defined(CH_CHACHA_VECTOR)
